99% of recent models:
We trained this new cool model that is chatgpt-like!
Reality:
1) Meta trained it, you don't have license for it;
2) The dataset you used is distilled from OpenAI;
3) You did a fine-tune of the model, you don't have to change its name because of this;
4) Yes it runs fast in CPU, but is also 4-bit quantized, and you don't even cited the author of the lib that actually did this for you;
5) You did zero evaluations to back any of you claims of performance, it is more like "IhaveNoIdeaModel" than "ChatGPT-like" model;
6) You are not helping with democratization of ML, you are doing marketing.

